<title>SWEDEN: Electrolux says Treschow to be new MD.</title>
<headline>Electrolux says Treschow to be new MD.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish appliance maker Electrolux said on Monday that Michael Treschow, currently managing director of industrial engineering group Atlas Copco, was to replace Leif Johansson as managing director.  </p>
<p>Electrolux said Treschow had worked for Atlas Copco since 1975, the last six years as president and chief executive.</p>
<p>&quot;Treschow will assume responsibilities in connection with Electrolux annual general meeting on April 29,&quot; Electrolux said in a statement.</p>
<p>Johansson is moving to AB Volvo where he will replace Soren Gyll. He had been president of Electrolux since 1991 and chief executive since 1994.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
